R&C patch 7062: PAD_SCRIPT anchors -- scripted input timed from a game event (ToD regression gate).
ToD's scripted regression played its in-level inputs at fixed wall-clock seconds, but Metropolis' control starts at a
different second in every build (281 s in tods-7049-reg, 247 s in tods-7054-reg), so the same inputs walked Ratchet
into different places and the gate's restart / Lua-pair counts moved with the build's load speed (base main failed the
gate too, 2026-11-11). A script token "@fs:TEXT" (libs/input/pad_script_anchor.h) now starts an anchored part: every
event after it is timed in seconds after the game's first cellFsOpen of a path containing TEXT (found or not; seen
through KZ3 4024's pre-open hook, an earlier hook chained), resolved at the next pad poll so the times stay on the pad
clock. Anchored events never fire before the anchor. Logs: "[cellPad] PAD_SCRIPT: anchor '@fs:TEXT', N event(s) timed
from it" at load and "[cellPad] script anchor '@fs:TEXT' fired at T s (pad clock)" once; fired anchored events print
t=@+T. One anchor per script (a second one, an unknown kind or an empty text count as unparsable). The keyboard
script (KZ3_KB_SCRIPT, 4026) parses anchors but has no hook: its anchored events would never fire.
Host test port/rc/tests/run_pad_anchor_test.sh runs cellPad.c's own parser and player (cut from the patched file):
parse, play before and after the anchor, a non-matching open, a second open, the unanchored control, and
tools/pad/tods-newgame-anchored.txt (336 events, 330 anchored, none bad). Mutants (anchor ignored, anchor re-fired,
every event anchored) each fail it.

